WEBVTT

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:09.340
Every WaveMaker React Native app is
bundled by Metro with a configuration

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.500
WaveMaker sets up for you.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.520
A custom Metro configuration lets you
add your own settings on top of it.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:26.740
In Studio, add a file named
custommetro.config.js to the web

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.280
app folder. Export an async function.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.300
It receives WaveMaker's Metro config,
so you change only what you need.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:41.240
Here, we add Lottie as an asset type
and point an alias at a library.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.820
Always finish by returning the config.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.260
On the next build, WaveMaker copies your
file into the generated app and applies it

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.220
after its own settings.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:57.860
No file? The app builds with
WaveMaker's defaults just as before.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:06.060
Use it for any metro setting WaveMaker
doesn't set for you, from the resolver and

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.600
transformer to caching or a
library's metro plug-in like Sentry.

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:16.840
Edit the config you're given instead of
replacing it so built-ins like SVG support

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:21.820
keep working. One file and
metro builds your app your way.
